<section>
	<header>
		<h1>Automatic Updater</h1>
	</header>
	<article ng-show="!card_loaded" class="loading-container">
		<i class="spinner-editor"></i>
	</article>
	<article ng-show="card_loaded && !latest_version">
		<p>
			We could not connect to the DeskPRO servers to fetch information about the latest version.
		</p>
		<p>
			Try refreshing the page to try again. If you continue to receive this message, you can install
			updates manually as described below.
		</p>
	</article>
	<article ng-show="card_loaded && latest_version">
		<section>
			<p>
				You are currently running DeskPRO version #{{ ng_var('version_info.build_name') }}. The newest version available is #{{ ng_var('latest_version.build_num_base') }}.
			</p>
			<p>
				The automatic updater will install the newest version of DeskPRO for you by just clicking the button below.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h3>Backup Options</h3>
			<p>
				It is recommended you enable backups so that in the very unlikely event a problem occurs,
				you will be able to revert to the backup.
			</p>
			<label>
				<input type="checkbox" ng-model="opt.db_backup" /> Back up the database before installing the upgrade
			</label>
			<br/>
			<label>
				<input type="checkbox" ng-model="opt.file_backup" /> Back up the current DeskPRO source files before installing the upgrade
			</label>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h3>Time Delay</h3>
			<p>
				You may wish to delay the start of the automatic update. This will show an alert notice to any online agents,
				giving them time to finish their work before the update starts.
			</p>
			<label>
				<input type="radio" ng-model="opt.time_type" value="now" /> Start the update now
			</label>
			<label style="margin-left: 10px;">
				<input type="radio" ng-model="opt.time_type" value="delay" /> Start the update in <span ng-show="opt.time_type != 'delay'">...</span>
			</label>
			<span ng-show="opt.time_type == 'delay'">
				<input type="text" class="form-control" ng-model="opt.delay" style="padding: 1px; margin: 0; font-size: 11px; width: 45px; display: inline-block; height: auto;" /> minutes
			</span>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h3>User Offline Message</h3>
			<p>
				Enter the message to show on the user portal about the helpdesk being unavailable.
			</p>
			<input type="text" ng-model="opt.user_message" class="form-control" style="width: 80%" ng-init="opt.user_message = 'The helpdesk is undergoing routine maintenance. We will be back in about 10 minutes.'" />
		</section>
	</article>
	<footer ng-show="card_loaded && latest_version">
		<div ng-show="!is_loading">
			<button class="btn btn-primary" ng-click="Home.startUpgrade();">Start the automatic update <i class="fa fa-arrow-circle-right"></i></button>
		</div>
		<div ng-show="is_loading">
			<i class="spinner-flat"></i>
		</div>
	</footer>
</section>
<div class="alert alert-info" style="margin-top: 25px;">
	<p>
		The preferred way to update DeskPRO is by using the automatic update tool above. But in some server enviornments,
		using this tool is not possible. For example, strict file permissions may prevent the automatic updater from working.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you cannot use the automatic update tool, you can use the CLI update tool instead which will
		install the updates with a single command on the command-line. Refer to the DeskPRO knowledgebase for more information:
	</p>
	<p>
		<i class="fa fa-globe"></i> <a href="https://support.deskpro.com/kb/articles/156">Installing Updates</a><br/>
		<i class="fa fa-globe"></i> <a href="https://support.deskpro.com/kb/articles/135">Manually Installing Updates</a>
	</p>
</div>
